<title>BELGIUM: EU Commission says cereals intervention normal.</title>
<headline>EU Commission says cereals intervention normal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cereals offered into intervention are average for the time of year and no dramatic changes are expected in the level of export refunds, a European Commission official told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Farmers are offering only normal amounts of cereals into intervention this week and there will be little effect on refunds,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Currently the European Union has 327,870 tonnes of soft wheat in intervention with 10,495 tonnes offered this week.</p>
<p>Barley in intervention stands at 23,121 tonnes in intervention with 126,054 offfered this week.</p>
<p>Rye in intervention stands at 241,633 tonnes with a further 85,712 tonnes offered this week.</p>
<p>All intervention stock figures exclude amounts accepted for export tender. --Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
